 ## Background
-Originated in the context of optimizing sparse-view 3D Gaussian Radiance Fields, specifically addressing the limitations of existing depth regularization strategies for NeRFs when applied to Gaussian fields [S1]. The method was proposed to prevent the geometry conflict caused by forcing Gaussian shapes to fit smooth monocular depth, which adversely affects quality [S1]. It is used in DNGaussian for improving detailed geometry reshaping in texture-rich regions [S1].
+Hard and Soft Depth Regularization was proposed in the context of optimizing sparse-view 3D Gaussian radiance fields [S1]. It addresses the limitations of existing depth regularization strategies for NeRFs, which create geometry conflicts in Gaussian fields by forcing Gaussian shapes to fit smooth monocular depth [S1]. The method is based on the principle that the basis of scene geometry lies in the position of Gaussian primitives rather than their shape [S1].
 
